      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a solid start, very classic. The tone is definitely heading in the right direction. \n\nHowever, looking at the internal metrics, the \"vocabulary richness\" score is actually a bit lower than we usually aim for with our flagship launches. I get that you don't want it to be unreadable, but our stakeholders really lean on that metric to justify the premium positioning of the brand. \n\nCould you try another version? Try to really push the descriptive depth. Make it feel even more lush and multifaceted. Just... try to find a way to bring that adjective count up significantly without making it look like a list. I'm really looking for that sweet spot where the prose stays elegant but the vocabulary becomes much more expansive and varied.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
